The given triangle has angles \(m\angle A = 28^\circ\), \(m\angle B = 74^\circ\) and \(m\angle C = 26^\circ\). The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \(180^\circ\). We can verify this for our triangle as follows:

\[ m\angle A + m\angle B + m\angle C = 28^\circ + 74^\circ + 26^\circ = 128^\circ + 26^\circ = 180^\circ \]

